+This rule is triggered when the delimiter of an ordered list item (the period
+in `1.` or the parenthesis in `1)`) doesn't match the configured style:
+
+```markdown
+1. Item
+2. Item
+
+1) Item
+2) Item
+```
+
+To fix this, use the same delimiter everywhere:
+
+```markdown
+1. Item
+2. Item
+
+1. Item
+2. Item
+```
+
+The `style` parameter can be `"period"` (`1.`), `"parenthesis"` (`1)`) or
+`"consistent"` (the default), in which case the first ordered list item in the
+document sets the style.
+
+Rationale: Consistent formatting makes it easier to understand a document.
